{number: 95}
{title: O Jesus, I Have Promised}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
O [G] Jesus, I have [C] promised to [G] serve Thee to the [D7] end;
Be [G] Thou forever [C] near me, my [G] Master [D7] and my [G] Friend:
I [D7] shall not fear the [G] battle if [C] Thou art by my [D7] side,
Nor [G] wander from the [C] pathway if [G] Thou wilt [D7] be my [G] Guide.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
O [G] let me feel Thee [C] near me; the [G] world is ever [D7] near;
I [G] see the sights that [C] dazzle, the [G] tempting [D7] sounds I [G] hear;
My [D7] foes are ever [G] near me, a-[C] round me and with-[D7] in;
But, [G] Jesus, draw Thou [C] nearer, and [G] shield my [D7] soul from [G] sin.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
O [G] Jesus, Thou hast [C] promised to [G] all who follow [D7] Thee,
That [G] where Thou art in [C] glory there [G] shall Thy [D7] servant [G] be;
And, [D7] Jesus, I have [G] promised to [C] serve Thee to the [D7] end;
O [G] give me grace to [C] follow, my [G] Master [D7] and my [G] Friend.
{end_of_verse}
